            "target_entity_instance": "discrete time steps (days)",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalFeature",
            "paragraph": "The main difference equation (discrete time steps, days) in our simulation describes the growth of individual krill animals over time, as a function of their present size, temperature, and available food. Using this equation, we modeled the growth of ~2000 individual krill organisms, together representative of the complete krill population in fishing Area 48 (66 106 tons, \u2192 each simulated krill \u2248 33 03 tons). In our model, each individual enters the population as a juvenile at a length of 7 millimeters, and then grows according to the equations described below in detail.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "krill predator prey model",
