            "relation": "HAS_SIMULATION_TYPE",
            "target_entity_instance": "transient",
            "target_entity_type": "SimulationType",
            "paragraph": "We next used the predator-prey model described in the methods to simulate the effects of krill fishing and climate change in Area 48 (as defined by the CCAMLR; Fig. 4). We simulated the development of the krill and predator populations for ten years, both under baseline conditions, with simulated climate change (sea ice reduction by 50%, and SST warming by 0.2\u00b0 C in ten years) and with a ten-fold increase in krill fishing. We also simulated a scenario with the combination of increased fishing and climate change.",
